---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/funding-rates/`;
const description =
  "How funding works on Aster: the rate formula, premium index, interval changes, the 15-second charge window, and how funding moves your liquidation price.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "Funding rates",
  alternativeHeadline: "Aster funding rates explained",
  name: "Aster funding rates explained",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Mechanics",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Perpetual futures" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Interest rate", sameAs: "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q179179" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Funding rate", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/perpetuals/fees-and-specs/funding-rate` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Mark price", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/perpetuals/fees-and-specs/mark-price` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Funding rates", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Aster Funding Rates — Formula, Interval and Liquidation Impact | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Funding rates" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-sky-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Mechanics</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Funding rates
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Funding is what keeps a perpetual close to spot. It is a peer-to-peer payment, not a fee Aster keeps, and it is
      charged on a schedule that can change without a separate announcement. For a leveraged position, funding is often
      the difference between a profitable hold and a slow loss.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> ·{" "}
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}trading/perpetuals/fees-and-specs/funding-rate`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">official funding docs</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="sign-heading">
    <h2 id="sign-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Which way it flows</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-emerald-300">Positive funding</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">The perp trades above the mark. Longs pay shorts. Being long has a carrying cost.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-rose-300">Negative funding</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">The perp trades below the mark. Shorts pay longs. Being short has a carrying cost.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="formula-heading">
    <h2 id="formula-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">The formula</h2>
    <div class="bg-brand-950/60 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
      <code class="block text-xs text-sky-200 leading-relaxed">
        F = [P + clamp(interest rate − P, 0.05%, −0.05%)] / (8 / N)
      </code>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
        P = average premium index; N = funding interval in hours; interest rate = 0.01% (0% for BNBUSDT).
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      The clamp limits how far the interest component can move. The divisor is what makes a 4-hour interval different
      from an 8-hour one: with N = 4, the result is divided by 2.
    </p>
    <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
      <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Aster's own example: ASTERUSDT at a 4-hour interval</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        F = [P + clamp(0.01% − P, 0.05%, −0.05%)] / 2. The premium index is sampled every 5 seconds and averaged with
        time weighting, so a single print does not set the rate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="amount-heading">
    <h2 id="amount-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What you actually pay</h2>
    <div class="bg-brand-950/60 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5">
      <code class="block text-xs text-sky-200">funding amount = position size × mark price × funding rate</code>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      A $10,000 position at a 0.01% rate pays $1 per interval. At 0.1% it pays $10. Over a week at a 4-hour interval, the
      second case is $420 — more than many traders expect from a "small" rate.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Funding is deducted from the Perps account balance. If the balance is insufficient, it can be taken from position
      margin, which moves the liquidation price. Aster does not charge or receive funding; it is transferred between
      traders.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="timing-heading">
    <h2 id="timing-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Timing details that surprise people</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      <li>There is a 15-second deviation between the actual time and when the fee is charged. Opening at 16:00:05 UTC may still incur that interval's funding.</li>
      <li>The interval can change when the rate hits its cap or floor, and there is no separate announcement for that change.</li>
      <li>The current rate and interval are shown on the real-time funding and funding history pages.</li>
      <li>Funding is calculated every block in 1001x, not on the 4/8-hour schedule used by Pro mode.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Real-time rate:{" "}
      <a href="https://www.asterdex.com/en/futures/futures-info/real-time-funding-rate" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Aster funding page ↗</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-rose-500/5 border border-rose-400/20 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-2" aria-labelledby="risk-heading">
    <h2 id="risk-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-sm text-rose-200 tracking-wide">Why it matters for risk</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      A position can be directionally right and still lose money to funding. In cross margin, funding on one position
      reduces the buffer for all of them. In 1001x, per-block funding is part of the liquidation calculation, so a
      static position drifts toward liquidation even when price is flat.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      See <a href="/aster-dex/liquidation-risk/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">liquidation mechanics</a> and{" "}
      <a href="/aster-dex/1001x/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">1001x</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-2">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
